Comment:
 This package bundles third-party components, which Debian Policy and the
 Fedora packaging guidelines ask a package to declare rather than hide. They
 are listed here in full.
 .
 /usr/bin/fermix is a single self-extracting executable produced by Burrito.
 It contains, in addition to this project's own compiled BEAM code:
 .
   * Erlang/OTP, including the ERTS, linked against musl libc, distributed
     under the Apache License 2.0. Upstream: https://www.erlang.org
   * The Elixir standard library, Apache License 2.0.
     Upstream: https://elixir-lang.org
   * musl libc, MIT License. Upstream: https://musl.libc.org
   * OpenSSL, statically linked into the ERTS crypto driver, Apache License
     2.0. Upstream: https://www.openssl.org
   * The Burrito wrapper and its embedded XZ decoder (public domain).
     Upstream: https://github.com/burrito-elixir/burrito
   * The Elixir and Erlang libraries this project depends on, each under its
     own licence; `fermix capabilities` and the project's mix.lock name them.
 .
 /usr/lib/fermix/runtime-payload/libc-musl-<digest>.so is the musl libc
 dynamic loader the bundled ERTS was linked against, MIT License. The package
 configuration step copies it to /var/lib/fermix/runtimes/<digest>/libc-musl.so
 and leaves it there when the package is removed, because a Fermix release that
 is still running asks the kernel for that exact file.
 .
 /usr/lib/fermix/cosign is a static build of Sigstore cosign, Apache License
 2.0, used to verify plugin and release signatures.
 Upstream: https://github.com/sigstore/cosign
